  "findings": [
    "All three runs reached 96 h with exit code zero. Native validation accepted 291 numbered states, 297 field states including initial and post-loop terminal states, and 588 medium-ledger rows. Independent reconstruction checked 900 scalar values and 1194 signed scalar/spatial paired differences.",
    "Halving the integration step at fixed fine grid lowered time-averaged target counts in every seed by 22.0417, 9.1146 and 42.8750 targets. Endpoints declined from 284, 295 and 306 to 256, 279 and 232. The endpoint ranges are disjoint, but N3 ranges are descriptive and are not confidence intervals.",
    "No primary count screen was triggered against the prespecified reference envelope. This does not establish negligible paired changes: seed 2 differs by 74 targets at 96 h, and its largest hourly difference is 89. The envelope screen and same-seed differences answer different questions; the original tolerance is preserved.",
    "There are 2, 12 and 12 primary field-screen entries. The 24 h maximum IFNG/TNF exposure is flagged in every seed, but the same-seed IFNG maximum changes have mixed signs. Identical IFNG and TNF fields duplicate the numerical observation; the entries do not establish independent biological pathway effects.",
    "All three refined endpoints remain above the original coarse-grid N3 endpoint range of 147–164. The refined endpoint excesses relative to matched original seeds are 98, 115 and 85 targets. Reducing this transport step therefore does not eliminate the previously observed grid-associated shift.",
    "The mean integrated target burden can conceal large trajectory changes. Against the original coarse grid, signed time-averaged differences are -3.3750, -10.9635 and -4.1406 targets, whereas time-averaged absolute differences are 67.2917, 82.1406 and 56.5885 targets. All three differences change sign over time.",
    "Spatial readouts remain numerically dependent. At 48 h, the fraction of living effectors inside the initial target hull is 0.331–0.404, compared with 0.454–0.583 at the previous fine-grid step and 0.974–0.992 in the original coarse-grid runs. A static initial hull and present cell contacts are distinct observables.",
    "All residual targets are assigned Ag-negative states; the refined endpoints retain 14, 23 and 20 unprimed targets. These are classifications within the implemented model, not experimentally measured mechanism fractions.",
    "For TE2, the refined local-entry scenario still has greater time-averaged target burden and greater 96 h residual counts than the available fine-grid 2D and 3D runs in all three seeds. These diagnostic comparisons use diffusion steps of 0.005 min for local entry and 0.01 min for 2D/3D. All six hourly differences change sign. The result supports a conditional configured-scenario comparison, not a universal ordering at every time or a pure dimensionality effect.",
    "This check provides a second integration step at the fine grid; it does not provide a third grid level or establish the continuum limit. Quantitative grid-independent counts, exposure and spatial access remain unsupported. Numerical sensitivity must accompany the central comparative results."
  ],
